  data: {
    LLM: "Be aggressive with your bids if you have a high trump (Ace or King) and at least one other card of the same suit. Since you only have 5 cards, a single strong suit can carry the whole hand. If you aren't the bidder, your only goal is to 'break' the bid by taking just one trick.\n\nThe 'Overbid' Defense: If you have a solid hand (e.g., King and Queen of a suit) and someone bids 3, you should consider bidding 4 just to prevent them from taking the pot. Even if you fail, you prevent them from certain victory and force them to play defensively next round.\n\nCounting the BlÃ¼cher: Only bid Wellington or BlÃ¼cher if you hold the Ace and King of your lead suit. If someone else holds the Ace, they will almost certainly 'break' you on the first trick. Wellington is a psychological tool to scare away weaker 'Nap' bidders.",
